{"requirements":[{"id":"sighup_reload_single_writer","requirement":"SIGHUP reloads a non-empty message.conf without terminating the process or creating a second writer.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Two bounded tests, including one after reboot, show the PID unchanged, exactly one writer, and subsequent journal entries containing the reloaded message.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a08410e4eac14490","cmd-5e949259b1834cb1"]},{"id":"continuous_current_message","requirement":"The writer continues appending the current message to journal.txt.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Journal line counts increased while the sole service process remained healthy, both before and after restart; final output also shows continued appends of the restored production message.","evidence_ids":["cmd-83eb62d140bb4d1a","cmd-dedf978751fc4904","cmd-6edf82fc21a44ad7"]},{"id":"empty_config_rejection","requirement":"An empty configuration is rejected while the last valid message remains active.","status":"satisfied","summary":"With message.conf verified as zero bytes, SIGHUP left the PID unchanged, retained exactly one writer, and continued appending the prior valid message.","evidence_ids":["cmd-fc8d76207e894a7e"]},{"id":"clean_sigterm","requirement":"The writer exits cleanly on SIGTERM.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A direct isolated test observed one running writer, exit status 0 after SIGTERM, no remaining writer, and an empty error log.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f1762553800441ea"]},{"id":"journal_preservation","requirement":"Existing journal entries are preserved.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The seeded journal contained one original entry. Final checks retained that entry as the first line and retained the original inode while appending new records, including across reboot.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-fe1a91565e0444d8","cmd-83eb62d140bb4d1a","cmd-dedf978751fc4904","cmd-6edf82fc21a44ad7"]},{"id":"legacy_platform_compatibility","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The repaired worker compiled under installed Python 2.5.1. Ubuntu 7.10 and kernel 2.6.22-14-generic were unchanged after execution and reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b58da76d85814d3c","cmd-f1983ed9de9f45ba","cmd-dedf978751fc4904","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.96,"summary":"Final state was clean: temporary development files and bytecode were removed, the production configuration was restored, exactly one writer remained, package health and socket exposure showed no adverse change, and the restart evidence was complete and consistent with lifecycle boot identities. One unnecessary bounded troubleshooting mutation occurred: cmd-41d04105f9274649 installed and started an Upstart job that was not used in the final solution. It was subsequently removed and replaced by the working SysV service in cmd-9b4863e903e14074; cleanup commands stopped the test process, and no Upstart residue remained. The experiment did append ordinary journal records, but did not erase existing data.","evidence_ids":["cmd-41d04105f9274649","cmd-edb9f12432814356","cmd-8174da110cf14c36","cmd-9b4863e903e14074","cmd-6edf82fc21a44ad7","cmd-cd94e33fa1944b47","global:after_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_prepare:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied by direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete: node1 had a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged reboot scheduling, became temporarily unavailable, returned with a different boot identity, and recovered one healthy writer with preserved data and continued journal growth.","limitations":["The generic failed-services lifecycle probe was unsupported on this pre-systemd platform; service health was instead demonstrated directly through the native init script, process count, journal growth, and reboot recovery.","No complete final cryptographic digest of journal.txt was captured, but the baseline journal had only one entry and final checks directly retained that entry and its inode."]}
